{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789396863,"nonce":"lQ1cwzgAqKBhcgjRA6XRn27Vai8=","title":"AOT compares with == by identity when the class defines its own","message":"Under --aot, `a == b` on instances whose class defines `==` compares\nidentity; the interpreter and both JIT tiers dispatch the operator.\nSpec corpus under AOT: hatch-color (Color constructors, hex, lerp),\nhatch-datetime (Duration comparisons, same instant different\noffsets), hatch-io (Buffer equality), hatch-math (NumRange\nequality) — 9 cases, every one an `expected false toBe true` on a\ncustom `==`. The same on either fiber backing. The LLVM tier had the\nsame shape of bug (4ff2c5b): the flag that says a class defines the\noperator has to be read from the class before the identity fast path.","files":null}]}